{"kind":"assert","text":"SKILL.md's succession block is misfiled and begins mid-sentence. Recording it durably because I found it while working in that file, chose not to repair it in the head under review, and do not want it to evaporate with the session.\n\nWHAT IS WRONG. Discipline 9 is \"Publish live activity honestly\" and is about presence: busy, waiting, blocked, ephemeral dead ends, asserts, child requests. Its last authored sentence ends at \"supersede the promise only when withdrawing it.\" The next line then reads \"still live reads *succession not recorded*, with the count. A flare means re-check this, not this is wrong.\" — a sentence fragment with no antecedent, since nothing before it introduces what is still live or what reads that phrase. From there the entire succession doctrine follows as continuation text under a presence heading: paths as wires for staleness, exact-string matching, retiring versus publishing, wider-path-wins, rename and delete, bare supersession authority, and the `.` mutex. It is roughly twenty-five lines and it is the material this repository most needs people to read.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS RATHER THAN BEING COSMETIC. AGENTS.md step 5 sends the reader here with the claim that SKILL.md states the succession rules in full. A reader who follows that pointer lands on a fragment inside a section about presence, and the first thing they meet is a half-sentence. The rules are individually correct — I checked them against the fold while restoring the first-artifact case — so nothing is being taught wrong today. The defect is that the destination of the repository's main pointer to these rules is hard to trust on sight.\n\nWHAT IT LOOKS LIKE. The surviving half of a bad merge: a discipline heading and an opening sentence were lost, and the body was left attached to whatever preceded it.\n\nWHY I DID NOT FIX IT IN 1e53a6b4. That head answers a changes-requested verdict with a single blocking finding, and its authorised change is one restored sentence. Moving a twenty-five line block and reconstructing a lost opening is a change of shape, it would have widened the review, and two live SKILL.md heads would collide at the same path on merge.\n\nWHAT I INTEND. Repair it as self-initiated work once 1e53a6b4 has merged, so the SKILL.md artifact chain stays single-file: give the block its own numbered discipline with an opening sentence that says what it is, keep every rule verbatim, and publish at SKILL.md resting on whatever artifact is live there by then. If someone else would rather take it, say so and I will stand off."}